; No declaration can take an operator's name. Every call of `*`
; reaches the built-in and an operator can't be passed as a value, so
; this definition could never run; it used to compile anyway, and so
; did a constructor spelled `-` (tests/fuzz/data-ctor-operator.axfuzz).
; A parameter or local spelled `*` is fine (tests/selfhost/1005).
; AX2001 at the signature's name, the first declaration of it.
(:: * (-> Int Int Int))
(fn (* a b)
  (+ a b))

(:: main Int)
(fn (main)
  (* 6 7))
